"""Append evidence-backed Tasks 3-8 to the assignment report."""
from pathlib import Path
import json


def append_sections(g):
    p,h,page,t,image=g['para'],g['heading'],g['page'],g['table'],g['image']
    root=g['ROOT']; f=root/'outputs/full_assignment'
    if not f.exists(): f=root/'submission/evidence/full_assignment'
    e=f/'evidence'; s=f/'screenshots'
    j=lambda x:json.loads(Path(x).read_text())
    assert j(e/'FINAL_VERIFICATION.json')['all_required_tasks_verified'], 'Complete verification is required'
    def shot(name,caption,height=300):image(s/(name+'.png'),caption,height)
    api='https://shiny-memory-g4467vr6gq7pc97pw-8001.app.github.dev'
    page('Task 3 - Experiment tracking and model registry')
    h('3.1 - Local MLflow tool lab')
    p('A local MLflow server uses a SQLite backend and a separate artifact directory. Two actual Fashion-MNIST runs change only Adam learning rate (0.01 versus 0.001), using 1,024 training and 256 validation examples, a 32-unit dense layer, batch 64, and three epochs. This small tool lab is distinct from the Task 2 Keras Tuner lab.')
    local=j(f/'local_toy_runs.json')
    t([['Learning rate','Validation loss','Validation accuracy','Run ID']]+[[r['learning_rate'],f"{r['val_loss']:.5f}",f"{r['val_accuracy']:.4f}",r['run_id']] for r in local],[65,85,90,253],True)
    p('For this fixed three-epoch budget, 0.01 gives lower validation loss and higher validation accuracy. This does not establish the best learning rate for another architecture, seed, or training duration. Per-epoch metrics, parameters, a loss plot, and the saved model are logged.')
    shot('mlflow-local','Local MLflow UI: two completed toy runs, with experiment context.')
    page('3.2 - DagsHub remote tracking')
    p('The same tool lab was run again against HayyanHaider/23L-0727_A2_Ops.mlflow. Credentials are read from the ignored environment file. The remote service stores real runs and artifacts; local JSON files are supporting exports. Random seeds and data version tags make provenance visible.')
    shot('mlflow-toy','DagsHub-hosted MLflow toy experiment: two actual remote runs.')
    page('3.3 - Manual callbacks and TensorFlow autologging')
    p('MlflowEpochLogger sends every epoch metric with its epoch step. The separate autolog run calls mlflow.tensorflow.autolog before fit; the manual callback is omitted for that run. Both methods record training and validation behavior. Run tags include the source commit, DVC pointer hash, seed, project, and logging method. Model files, actual learning curves, split manifests, and the exact tracking environment lock accompany the runs.')
    p('The original Colab experiments are also uploaded with explicit-historical-import tags. Their saved epoch CSVs, original stage settings, curves, and checkpoints are preserved. Those imports are not represented as live autologging. The six additional training runs below are actual live instrumentation demonstrations.')
    shot('mlflow-manual','A live manually logged run: parameters, tags, and recorded metric values.')
    page('3.3 - TensorFlow autologging evidence')
    p('This separate live run uses TensorFlow autologging with the manual epoch callback omitted. Its five training and validation metric steps were verified through the remote API. Framework-generated optimizer parameters and validation metrics accompany the configured learning rate and dropout.')
    shot('mlflow-autolog','The TensorFlow autolog run: framework-generated epoch metrics and parameters.')
    page('3.4 - Six controlled validation-only runs')
    p('The original held-out evaluation had already happened. To avoid selecting a new model against exposed test results, all six diagnostic runs use only the original 680 training and 146 validation examples. Each initializes the same original frozen-head checkpoint, caches its 1,280-dimensional MobileNetV2 features, and trains a dense head for five epochs, batch 32. Backbone and BatchNorm stay frozen, with augmentation disabled. Learning rate or dropout changes one factor at a time relative to the baseline. No test inference is performed, and none of these runs is promoted.')
    runs=j(f/'dagshub_instrument_runs.json')
    t([['Method','LR','Dropout','Train loss','Val loss','Val accuracy']]+[[r['logging'],r['learning_rate'],r['dropout'],f"{r['loss']:.4f}",f"{r['val_loss']:.4f}",f"{r['val_accuracy']:.4f}"] for r in runs],[68,65,65,95,95,105],True)
    image(e/'tracking-comparison.png','Actual remote run histories: validation loss over five epochs.',245)
    p('Increasing learning rate from 0.001 to 0.01 reduces training loss but increases final validation loss to 0.7244, consistent with poorer validation generalization at this budget. The 0.0001 run adapts more slowly. Removing dropout increases training fit, while validation loss stays near the baseline. Dropout 0.5 and 0.7 do not improve final loss here. Small differences near 0.534 are not persuasive without repeated seeds. Original tuned champion loss 0.47383 remains better, but it also adapts backbone layers, so this is not a controlled architecture comparison.')
    page('3.4 - Remote six-run comparison')
    p('The native remote comparison contains all six live diagnostic runs. The table and loss chart on the preceding page use the actual five-epoch histories and provide the controlled learning-rate/dropout comparison. IDs and full parameter dictionaries are supplied in remote-mlflow-audit.json.')
    shot('mlflow-comparison','Remote experiment view containing the six distinct diagnostic configurations.',270)
    page('3.5 - Artifacts and model registry')
    shot('mlflow-artifacts','Actual remote artifact browser: model and reproducibility evidence.',285)
    p('The artifact browser confirms stored model files, environment, split manifests, loss curves and epoch histories. Split manifests preserve membership; the DVC version tag identifies dataset metadata, while the environment lock identifies the actual tracking runtime.')
    page('3.5 - Registry promotion and alias inference')
    p('The registry contains version 1 from the original frozen-head checkpoint and version 2 from the original winning tuned checkpoint. The champion alias resolves to version 2. scripts.predict_by_alias is a separate process: it resolves models:/23L-0727_A2_Ops@champion, loads the model, exports it, and predicts a training example. The registry export is reserialized, so its file hash differs; all 262 weight arrays were verified exactly equal to the original deployment champion. Release provisioning verifies the original file SHA-256 before use.')
    shot('mlflow-registry','DagsHub model registry: two actual versions and the champion alias.',290)
    t([['Check','Observed result'],['Registry alias','champion -> version 2'],['Independent alias prediction','Known-real training sample: Real; AI score 0.21879'],['Registry/release parity','262 weight arrays exactly equal'],['Remote run count','20 completed runs: 2 toy + 6 live diagnostics + 12 original imports']],[140,353])
    page('Task 4 - Flask inference application')
    h('4.1 - Model loading and preprocessing')
    p('visionguard.inference separates prediction from routes. Each Gunicorn worker loads the champion once at application startup with compile=False, verifies its metadata hash, and warms it up. Requests reuse that predictor. Images are decoded in memory, EXIF orientation is applied, and RGB pixels are resized with aspect-preserving zero padding to 224 x 224 using TensorFlow bilinear antialiasing. Embedded MobileNet normalization maps the resulting 0-255 values to [-1,1]; inference disables training augmentation.')
    p('The sigmoid is the AI score. The validation-selected threshold 0.6806868 determines the label. Displayed confidence is the score for the predicted class, with an explicit calibration caveat. It is not a forensic guarantee. Filename sanitization removes path components, and raw uploads are not written to disk.')
    h('4.2 - Routes and user flow')
    t([['Route','Behavior'],['GET /','Upload form; accepted types and limit'],['POST /predict','HTML result with decision, score, model version and request ID'],['POST /api/predict','API-key authenticated multipart request; JSON response'],['GET /history','Recent persisted records'],['GET /health','Database readiness, deployment mode, model version, debug state']],[145,348])
    shot('flask-home','Actual local upload page with project and student context.',300)
    page('4.3 - Results, validation failures, and configuration')
    shot('flask-direct-result','Actual HTML response from resident-model inference; model version and score are visible.',230)
    p('The live HTTP smoke test accepted the real and AI demonstration PNGs. It also exercised an unsupported .exe extension (400), a corrupt PNG (400), and an upload over 5 MB (413). Decoder format is checked as well as extension, so renaming arbitrary bytes to .png is rejected. A decoded-pixel limit prevents very large decompressed images. Errors produce friendly responses without stack traces; unexpected failures are logged and return 503.')
    shot('flask-failures','Saved actual HTTP error responses rendered for inspection; all three failures were verified over HTTP.',220)
    p('MODEL_PATH, MODEL_METADATA_PATH, MODEL_THRESHOLD, MAX_UPLOAD_BYTES, DATABASE_URL, INFERENCE_API_URL, and INFERENCE_API_KEY are environment settings. .env.example contains placeholders; the real .env is ignored and excluded from the archive. Flask debug is false and Gunicorn provides the serving process.')
    page('Task 5 - Persistent prediction history')
    p('SQLAlchemy stores every successful prediction transaction. The production-like Compose configuration uses PostgreSQL 17 on its internal service network. A local SQLite database is available for a standalone run and the Codespace API. A UUID identifies each request; UTC time, sanitized filename, label, AI score, predicted-class confidence, threshold, model version, model hash, and latency preserve what happened and which model produced it. Failed uploads create no prediction rows.')
    p('The history route queries recent records rather than maintaining a process-local list. Raw image bytes and API keys are not part of the prediction table. Filenames can still reveal information, so a real production system would need retention and access controls.')
    shot('flask-history','Actual prediction history page, populated by successful requests.',270)
    page('5 - PostgreSQL records and restart persistence')
    shot('docker-database','Actual SQL query output and persistence checks from the PostgreSQL container.',260)
    p('The container stack was removed with compose down and started again without deleting volumes. The same two records existed before and after (2 -> 2), confirming persistence in the named PostgreSQL volume. Removing the volume with down -v would intentionally remove that database and is not part of normal restart instructions.')
    page('Task 6 - Containers, Compose, and CI/CD')
    h('6.1 - Docker warm-up')
    p('A disposable BusyBox container demonstrated image pull, run with a published HTTP port, container listing, HTTP access, logs, shell execution, stop, container removal, persistent volume recovery, image removal, and volume cleanup. The transcript records actual commands and their outputs. A file written in the first container remained readable in a second container mounting the same named volume.')
    shot('docker-warmup','Actual Docker warm-up transcript, first portion: image, container, port, logs, and shell.',280)
    shot('docker-warmup-2','Actual Docker warm-up transcript, continuation: stop, removal, volume recovery and cleanup.',260)
    page('6.2 - Dockerfile, image layers, and optimization')
    p('The image starts from Python 3.11 slim Bookworm. Dependency installation precedes application COPY, allowing cached dependency layers when code changes. TensorFlow is installed without CUDA extras; no GPU runtime is required. The application runs as UID 10001, exposes the web port, and has a health check. Gunicorn uses one worker with two threads to avoid loading multiple model copies into memory.')
    p('.dockerignore excludes credentials, virtual environments, Git/DVC caches, raw/processed datasets, outputs, notebooks, submission files, and local model binaries. The champion is supplied as a read-only bind mount, keeping large models and secrets out of image layers. PostgreSQL credentials are environment values, not baked into the Dockerfile.')
    t([['Measurement','Baseline','Optimized'],['Docker CLI displayed image size','3.03 GB','2.31 GB'],['Change','pip cache retained','--no-cache-dir; same serving packages']],[160,166,167])
    p('Under the same local Docker image accounting, removing the pip download cache saves approximately 0.72 GB (24%). TensorFlow and its dependencies still dominate the image; further slimming would need dependency/runtime evaluation. Docker inspect returned a different size accounting (779,569,988 vs 428,014,781 bytes), so these figures are not mixed with the CLI comparison.')
    shot('docker-images','Actual image-size and layer output; dependency layer dominates.',270)
    page('6.3 - Multi-service Compose and operations')
    p('compose.yaml defines web and db services. The web app connects to hostname db rather than localhost. PostgreSQL pg_isready gates web startup through a health dependency; a named volume retains its data. The database has no host-published port. Web binds to localhost, and the model mount is read-only. A fresh .env plus model files is sufficient for docker compose up --build -d. The demonstration used WEB_PORT=8002 because the standalone Flask process already occupied 8000.')
    shot('docker-compose','Actual service status, web UID, and network/port evidence.',270)
    page('6.3 - Deliberate failure and recovery')
    p('Stop/start/restart, service logs, and shell execution in both services were exercised. A deliberate MODEL_PATH=/models/missing.keras override caused a real startup failure with FileNotFoundError. Restoring the correct mount path and recreating web returned health status ok. Failure evidence is retained separately from the corrected healthy state.')
    shot('docker-failure','Actual deliberate missing-model failure, followed by repair and successful health response.',270)
    page('6.4 - GitHub Actions: red, green, and project checks')
    p('The separate ci-toy repository tests Python 3.11 and 3.12. Its first commit implements addition incorrectly as subtraction, causing the unit test to fail. A second commit fixes addition; both matrix jobs pass. These are real GitHub-hosted workflow executions, not simulated status badges.')
    shot('ci-red','Actual failing toy workflow; the accompanying log records the deliberate assertion failure.',265)
    shot('ci-green','Actual passing toy workflow after the fix; Python version matrix succeeds.',265)
    page('6.4 - Main project CI')
    p('Main project CI installs serving/test dependencies, performs critical-module Ruff checks, runs meaningful Flask validation/inference/history tests, and builds the Docker image. Ten tests pass locally; the main GitHub-hosted workflow also succeeds. The README links its live status badge. The test predictor is deterministic, while separate HTTP checks exercise the real saved model.')
    shot('ci-main','Actual successful project CI, including the Docker image build.',270)
    page('Task 7 - Cloud model API')
    h('7.1 - Deployment steps and endpoint')
    p('GitHub Codespaces was used under the user-approved free allowance: HayyanHaider Pro, two cores, Southeast Asia. Billing showed minimal included usage; no paid machine was selected. The existing repository was opened in a Codespace, its own source folder trusted, and requirements-serve.txt installed. scripts.provision_model downloaded the original champion from the project release and verified SHA-256. scripts.start_cloud started Gunicorn on 0.0.0.0:8001 with API_ONLY=true, a workspace SQLite history database, and the API key supplied through a Codespaces secret.')
    shot('cloud-terminal','Actual cloud terminal: provisioned model, matching hash, and successful local API health.',300)
    p('Port 8001 is forwarded with HTTP to the backend and HTTPS at the public boundary. Public prediction requests require X-API-Key; the unauthenticated health route reveals only readiness information. The key is not included in report, screenshots, repository, collection, or ZIP. All other routes are protected in API-only mode.')
    shot('cloud-public','Actual Codespaces port configuration and public forwarded address.',250)
    p('<b>API base URL:</b> '+api+'<br/><b>Prediction:</b> POST /api/predict, multipart field image, X-API-Key header.<br/><b>Health:</b> GET /health.')
    page('7.2 - Postman collection and independent network test')
    p('The supplied Postman collection runs through Newman, Postman\'s official command-line runner. It checks public health, known-real and known-AI PNG requests, response schema/scores/model version/request ID, and rejection without a key. API_URL and INFERENCE_API_KEY are injected at runtime; exported evidence omits request authentication headers.')
    shot('cloud-postman','Actual Postman/Newman verification summary from a GitHub-hosted runner, independent of the local network.',295)
    cloud=j(e/'http-cloud/results.json')
    t([['Request','HTTP status','Observed outcome']]+[[r['filename'],r['status'],r.get('response',{}).get('label',r.get('response',{}).get('error',''))] for r in cloud['cases']],[125,75,293],True)
    page('7.2 - Independent-network workflow')
    shot('cloud-workflow','Successful external-network workflow in the project repository.',250)
    p('A separate GitHub Actions workflow executes the collection against the public URL. Its successful run and sanitized JSON artifact demonstrate access from a second network. Local HTTP verification separately sends two valid images and the three invalid cases to the deployed model, without recalculating held-out evaluation metrics.')
    p('<b>Availability limit.</b> Codespaces is an on-demand development host, not an always-on production service. Idle timeout can stop the API; restart the Codespace, run python -m scripts.start_cloud if needed, and set port 8001 public again before grading. Visibility may revert to private after restart. The README documents these steps. Keep an API key private and share a grading credential separately if required.')
    page('Task 8 - Local Flask to cloud API integration')
    p('The local Flask app sets INFERENCE_API_URL to the public Codespaces URL and uses the matching key from its ignored environment. In remote mode it does not load the local predictor. It validates the upload, sends the in-memory multipart file to /api/predict with a 10-second connection/90-second response timeout, checks required response fields, persists the result, and renders it. Upstream errors produce a friendly 503; no silent local-model fallback masks a failed cloud call.')
    shot('integration-health','Actual local health endpoint: remote_api mode and ready history database.',180)
    shot('integration-real','Actual local HTML result obtained through the deployed cloud API: known-real input.',255)
    page('8 - Second input through the cloud API')
    p('The AI-labelled training sample reaches the same remote champion. It is classified as Real: an AI score around 0.5264 falls below the validation-selected threshold. The outcome is retained as a model error; a successful HTTP request is not proof of a correct class decision.')
    shot('integration-ai','Actual local HTML result obtained through the deployed cloud API: known-AI input.',255)
    page('8 - Request records and integration interpretation')
    shot('integration-history','Actual local history containing both cloud-backed request results.',285)
    p('The known-AI demonstration input is classified as Real (AI score about 0.5264, below the 0.6807 threshold). This is a model error, retained in the evidence. Transport success does not imply classification correctness.')
    p('Both demonstration inputs come from the training split and are supplied only to show request/response behavior. Their results are not a new accuracy estimate. The model label, score, threshold, version and hash identify the same original champion used in Task 2. The local history receives its own request UUID and UTC timestamp, so local records can be distinguished from the remote API\'s request records.')
    p('Local and cloud validation tests confirm successful predictions and expected 400/413 errors. The independent-network Postman run verifies authentication rejection as well. PostgreSQL persistence, genuine model execution, cloud transport, and UI rendering are exercised separately, so a mocked unit test is not the only evidence for the final system.')
    page('Submission map, reproduction, and limitations')
    t([['Deliverable','Contents/use'],['23L-0727_VisionGuard.pdf','Complete report with Tasks 1-8, figures, measured results and disclosure.'],['23L-0727_A2_Submission.zip','Source, model + metadata, executed notebook, selected training outputs, manifests, real verification logs, clean screenshots, Postman collection and report.'],['GitHub main + dvc-toy','Source/CI and separate two-version DVC lab history.'],['DagsHub project','Mirrored source, 20 MLflow runs, model registry and artifacts.']],[155,338])
    p('For a fresh local serving run: unpack the ZIP; copy .env.example to .env; set fresh POSTGRES_PASSWORD and INFERENCE_API_KEY; leave INFERENCE_API_URL empty for resident inference; ensure models/champion.keras and champion.json exist; run docker compose up --build -d. Open http://localhost:8000. Use docker compose logs and /health for diagnostics. Do not use down -v when preserving history.')
    p('For cloud integration: resume the named Codespace and public port, configure its API key privately, set local INFERENCE_API_URL and the same key, then recreate web. Reproduce training from the original dataset using the saved split lists and original environment; do not retune against the exposed test set. DVC recovery is demonstrated against permitted local-folder storage, not claimed as uploaded remote dataset bytes on DagsHub.')
    t([['Issue','Resolution / practical limit'],['macOS TensorFlow + old PyArrow conflict','Upgraded local PyArrow to 26.0.1; recorded actual lock. Serving has no MLflow/PyArrow dependency. MLflow 2.22.5 declares an older Arrow bound, so this is a local compatibility workaround.'],['ARM CPU TensorFlow package','Use tensorflow==2.21.0 without CUDA extras; actual ARM Docker and Linux Codespace inference verified.'],['Image accounting differs by command','Compare the same Docker CLI display before/after; retain inspect output separately.'],['Forwarding initially returned sign-in HTML','Changing the backend protocol reset visibility. Verified HTTP first, restored Public, then reran the external collection successfully.'],['On-demand cloud host','API stops when Codespace sleeps. Resume before grading; no always-on uptime claim.'],['Model limitations','Small single-source test, uncertain labels and possible source/near-duplicate leakage. Confidence is uncalibrated; human review remains necessary.']],[140,353],True)
    p('The optional Grad-CAM bonus was not attempted. All eight required tasks are covered; historical experiment imports and later validation-only diagnostics are explicitly distinguished from the original pre-test model selection.')
